        'title' => 'CTO Certificate Full Form: Consent to Operate Process',
        'description' => 'CTO means Consent to Operate. Who needs it, CTE vs CTO, documents, state pollution board fees, validity, renewal and CTO for mining units.',
        'lead' => 'CTO full form is Consent to Operate: the permission from the State Pollution Control Board to start and run a factory or facility after it has received Consent to Establish (CTE).',
        'sections' => [
            ['CTE vs CTO', '<table><thead><tr><th></th><th>Consent to Establish (CTE)</th><th>Consent to Operate (CTO)</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>When</td><td>Before construction or installing machinery</td><td>After the unit is built, before production starts</td></tr>
<tr><td>What the board checks</td><td>Site, layout, proposed process and pollution control plan</td><td>Pollution control systems installed and working as approved</td></tr>
<tr><td>Inspection</td><td>Site suitability</td><td>Installed ETP, STP, air pollution control equipment and stacks</td></tr>
