</tbody></table><p>Both are issued under the Water Act, 1974 and the Air Act, 1981. Read our <a href="/resources/blogs/cto-certificate-full-form-consent-to-operate">CTO certificate guide</a> for the Uttar Pradesh process.</p>'],
            ['CTO for mining', '<p>In mining, too, CTO means Consent to Operate. A mine or a mineral processing unit needs CTE and then CTO from the State Pollution Control Board, usually after it has received environmental clearance under the EIA Notification. Mining and ore beneficiation is in the red category, so the board inspects before granting consent and attaches conditions on dust control, water use, mine drainage and the overburden. Stone crushers and brick kilns have their own consent conditions and siting rules.</p>'],
            ['What is a CTO certificate?', '<p>A CTO certificate is the consent order issued by the State Pollution Control Board (or Pollution Control Committee in a union territory) allowing a unit to operate. It lists the products and capacity, the permitted discharge and emissions, monitoring and reporting conditions, and the validity. The unit must follow these conditions and file the returns the board asks for; operating without a valid CTO can lead to closure orders and prosecution.</p>'],
            ['Who needs CTO: red, orange, green and white categories', '<p>Industries are grouped by their pollution potential:</p><ul>
<li><strong>Red:</strong> highly polluting, such as chemicals, pharmaceuticals, tanneries, distilleries and mining. They need consent and the strictest scrutiny.</li>
<li><strong>Orange:</strong> moderately polluting. They need consent.</li>
<li><strong>Green:</strong> lightly polluting. They need consent, usually with longer validity and a simpler procedure.</li>
<li><strong>White:</strong> practically non-polluting. They are exempt from consent and only need to inform the board.</li>
</ul><p>Hospitals, hotels, large buildings and other non-industrial facilities can also need consent. See <a href="/services/indian-registration-compliances/environment-compliance/pollution-certificate-uttar-pradesh">pollution certificate in Uttar Pradesh</a> and the <a href="/services/indian-registration-compliances/factories-and-building/factory-license">factory licence</a>.</p>'],
        ],
        'faqs' => [
            ['What is the full form of CTO?', 'CTO stands for Consent to Operate. It is the permission a State Pollution Control Board grants under the Water and Air Acts for a unit to start and continue operating.'],
            ['How long is a CTO valid?', 'Boards have granted CTO for fixed periods by category, often longer for green and orange units than for red ones. A central amendment in January 2026 allows consent to remain valid until cancelled while the unit stays compliant, so check how your board applies it.'],
        ],
