        'key' => 'complete-guide-tec-certification-india-process-eligibility-benefits',
        'title' => 'TEC Certificate (MTCTE): Meaning, Process & Benefits',
        'description' => 'TEC certificate under MTCTE explained: full form, which telecom products need it, testing, certification schemes, process, timeline and benefits.',
        'answer' => '<p><strong>TEC full form is Telecommunication Engineering Centre</strong>, the technical body of the Department of Telecommunications (DoT). Under its MTCTE scheme, listed telecom and networking equipment must be tested at a designated lab and certified by TEC before it is sold, imported or used in India.</p>',
        'top' => [
            ['What is MTCTE?', '<p>MTCTE stands for <strong>Mandatory Testing and Certification of Telecommunication Equipment</strong>. It was introduced under the Indian Telegraph Rules and brought in product by product in phases. For each product, TEC publishes the essential requirements (ERs) it must meet, covering safety, EMC, radio, technical and, for many products, security requirements.</p><ul>
<li><strong>Testing:</strong> at a TEC-designated conformity assessment body (CAB) in India.</li>
<li><strong>Certification schemes:</strong> products are certified under the General Certification Scheme or the Simplified Certification Scheme, depending on their risk.</li>
<li><strong>Portal:</strong> applications are made on the MTCTE portal by the manufacturer, importer or their authorised Indian representative.</li>
</ul><p>Whether your product is covered is decided by TEC’s current product list and ERs, which grow with each phase. Read <a href="/resources/blogs/get-tec-certificate-before-importing-selling-using-tec-india">why you need a TEC certificate before importing</a>, or see <a href="/certification/india/tec-approval">TEC approval</a>.</p>'],
        ],
        'faqs' => [
            ['What is the full form of TEC?', 'TEC stands for Telecommunication Engineering Centre. It is the technical arm of the Department of Telecommunications and runs the MTCTE certification scheme.'],
            ['What is MTCTE certification?', 'MTCTE, or Mandatory Testing and Certification of Telecommunication Equipment, is the scheme under which notified telecom products must be tested in India against TEC’s essential requirements and certified before sale. Certificates are issued on the MTCTE portal.'],
            ['Is a TEC certificate mandatory for import?', 'Yes, for products notified under MTCTE. Customs and buyers check for the certificate, and listed equipment cannot be sold, imported or used without it; products outside the list do not need one.'],
            ['How long does TEC certification take?', 'It usually takes one to three months: testing at a designated lab is the longest part, followed by the review on the MTCTE portal. Products under the Simplified Certification Scheme are generally certified faster than those under the General Certification Scheme.'],
        ],
    ],

