        'title' => 'PESO Online CNG Certificate Download: Login & Steps',
        'description' => 'How to download a PESO CNG cylinder certificate online: vehicle number search, CNG module login, GCT explained, fixes when it is not found, testing licence.',
        'answer' => '<p><strong>To download a CNG cylinder test certificate, open PESO’s online portal (online.peso.gov.in), choose Status, select Gas Cylinders Rules and then “Search CNG Certificate by Vehicle Number”.</strong> Enter the vehicle number, the owner’s name and the registered mobile number, verify with the OTP and save the report as a PDF. PESO asks drivers to check the certificate before refuelling, because cylinders that are due for testing must not be filled.</p>',
        'top' => [
            ['Step-by-step: download your CNG certificate', '<ol>
<li>Go to online.peso.gov.in and open the public domain search.</li>
<li>Choose <strong>Status</strong>.</li>
<li>Under the rules, select <strong>Gas Cylinders Rules</strong>.</li>
<li>Choose <strong>Search CNG Certificate by Vehicle Number</strong>.</li>
<li>Select the number format and enter the vehicle registration number, the owner’s full name and the registered mobile number, then complete the captcha.</li>
<li>Enter the OTP sent to the mobile number and choose <strong>View Report</strong>.</li>
<li>Save or print the certificate as a PDF and keep it with the vehicle papers.</li>
</ol><p>Menu names on the portal can change; if an option has moved, use the portal’s help section.</p>'],
            ['PESO CNG login and module explained', '<p>There are two different parts of the PESO portal:</p><ul>
<li><strong>Public search for vehicle owners:</strong> no login is needed. You search by vehicle number as described above.</li>
<li><strong>CNG Certificate Module (login):</strong> used by PESO-approved gas cylinder testing stations. The station logs in with the user ID it created for its own online approval, enters the test results for each cylinder and generates the certificate. Once generated, a certificate cannot be edited.</li>
</ul>'],
            ['What is PESO online GCT?', '<p>“GCT” is the portal’s gas cylinder testing module (online.peso.gov.in/PesoOnlineGCT), which is the login page of the CNG Certificate Module. It is for testing stations, not for vehicle owners. The module checks the results as they are entered; for example, permanent expansion above 10% or weight loss above 5% fails the cylinder.</p>'],
            ['Certificate not showing? Common fixes', '<ul>
<li>Enter the vehicle number in the right format, without spaces or dashes unless the form asks for them.</li>
<li>Enter the owner’s name exactly as it appears on the registration certificate, and the mobile number registered with the transport department.</li>
<li>If the test was done recently, ask the testing station whether it has generated the certificate on the portal.</li>
<li>Older tests done before the station started using the online module may not appear; the station can confirm.</li>
<li>If the certificate has expired, the cylinder is due for retesting at an approved station.</li>
</ul>'],
            ['How to get a CNG cylinder testing station licence', '<p>Cylinder testing stations are approved by PESO under the Gas Cylinders Rules, 2016. The applicant needs suitable premises, hydrostatic stretch testing and other test equipment, trained staff and a competent person, and applies online with drawings and equipment details. PESO inspects before granting approval. See <a href="/certification/india/peso-certification">PESO certification</a> or our guide on <a href="/resources/blogs/how-to-get-peso-certificate">how to get a PESO certificate</a>.</p>'],
        ],
        'faqs' => [
            ['How do I download my CNG certificate from PESO?', 'On online.peso.gov.in, choose Status, then Gas Cylinders Rules, then Search CNG Certificate by Vehicle Number. Enter the vehicle number, owner’s name and mobile number, verify the OTP and save the report as a PDF.'],
            ['What is GCT in PESO?', 'GCT is PESO’s online gas cylinder testing module, the login page of the CNG Certificate Module. Approved testing stations use it to enter test results and generate CNG cylinder certificates.'],
            ['Why is my CNG certificate not found?', 'Usually the vehicle number, owner name or mobile number does not match the records, or the testing station has not generated the certificate online yet. Check the details against your registration certificate, then ask the testing station.'],
            ['How long is a CNG cylinder test certificate valid?', 'On-board CNG cylinders must be retested at the interval set under the Gas Cylinders Rules, commonly every three years, and the certificate shows the next due date. Cylinders past their due date must not be refilled.'],
            ['How do I start a CNG cylinder testing centre?', 'You need PESO approval as a gas cylinder testing station under the Gas Cylinders Rules, 2016. Apply online with your premises layout, equipment and staff details; PESO inspects before granting approval.'],
