        'type' => 'service',
        'key' => 'certification/global-certifications/cb-iecee',
        'title' => 'CB Test Certificate & CB Scheme: Meaning, Validity, Cost',
        'description' => 'What a CB test certificate and CB report are, IECEE CB Scheme meaning, validity, how to verify it, and how one report supports BIS, CE and other approvals.',
        'lead' => 'A CB test certificate, issued under the IECEE CB Scheme, shows that a product meets an IEC safety standard. Together with its CB test report, it is accepted by certification bodies in more than 50 member countries.',
        'sections' => [
            ['CB test certificate vs CB test report', '<table><thead><tr><th></th><th>CB test certificate (CBTC)</th><th>CB test report (CBTR)</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>What it is</td><td>A one- or two-page certificate issued by a National Certification Body (NCB)</td><td>The full test record from a CB Testing Laboratory (CBTL)</td></tr>
<tr><td>Contents</td><td>Product, models, ratings, standard and edition, the report number</td><td>Every clause of the standard with results, photos, component list and national differences tested</td></tr>
<tr><td>Valid on its own?</td><td>No – only together with the report</td><td>Yes, as the evidence the other NCBs review</td></tr>
</tbody></table><p>Always send both to the body in the target country.</p>'],
            ['How to check a CB certificate in the IECEE database', '<p>CB test certificates are published in the IECEE online certificates database on iecee.org. Search by the certificate number, the holder or the manufacturer, and check that the standard edition, models and ratings match the product you are buying or certifying. A certificate missing from the database, or with different details, should be confirmed with the issuing NCB.</p>'],
            ['CB vs CE marking', '<p>A CB certificate is <strong>evidence</strong> that a product passed tests to an IEC standard. CE marking is a <strong>legal declaration</strong> by the manufacturer that the product meets EU law. They are often linked: a CB report that includes the European group differences is commonly used as test evidence for the Low Voltage Directive. But CE also needs EMC, RoHS, a technical file and a Declaration of Conformity, which a CB report does not cover. See <a href="/certification/emea/ce-certification">CE certification</a>.</p>'],
            ['Using a CB report for BIS, CE, UKCA and other approvals', '<ul>
<li><strong>EU (CE) and Great Britain (UKCA):</strong> used as safety test evidence in the technical file. See <a href="/certification/emea/ukca-certification">UKCA certification</a>.</li>
<li><strong>Gulf, Africa and Asia:</strong> many national schemes accept or require a CB report for safety approval, sometimes with local tests for plugs, voltage or climate.</li>
<li><strong>USA and Canada:</strong> certification bodies can use CB results to reduce testing for their own marks.</li>
<li><strong>India:</strong> BIS registration generally still needs testing at a BIS-recognised lab in India, but a CB report against <a href="/is-iec-62368-1">IS/IEC 62368-1</a> or a similar standard reduces design surprises.</li>
</ul>'],
            ['What is the IECEE CB Scheme?', '<p>The CB Scheme is run by the IECEE, the IEC’s system for conformity assessment of electrical equipment. Member countries agree to accept each other’s test results to IEC standards, so a product tested once by a CB Testing Laboratory and certified by a National Certification Body can use that report to get national approvals elsewhere, often without full retesting. Our guide <a href="/resources/blogs/cb-test-certificate-iecee-cb-scheme-explained">CB test certificate and the IECEE CB Scheme explained</a> covers it in more detail.</p>'],
        ],
        'faqs' => [
            ['What is a CB certificate?', 'A CB certificate, or CB test certificate, is issued by a National Certification Body under the IECEE CB Scheme to show a product meets an IEC safety standard. It is valid only together with the CB test report.'],
            ['What is the full form of CB in CB Scheme?', 'CB stands for Certification Body. The CB Scheme is the IECEE scheme for the mutual recognition of test certificates issued by National Certification Bodies.'],
            ['Is a CB certificate mandatory?', 'No. The CB Scheme is voluntary. It is used because it saves retesting when you need approvals in several countries, and some buyers and national schemes ask for it.'],
        ],
    ],

